    <DataNode elementId="CPD-14483" textLabel="glycyrrhetinate" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="MPDGHEJMBKOTSU-VOPRYAMFSA-M" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="500" centerY="780" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, zhang, O-28, hartmut">|FRAME: CPD-14483 &quot;Glycyrrhetinic acid&quot;| is a pentacyclic triterpenoid derivative of the |FRAME: CPD-6948| type obtained from the hydrolysis of |FRAME: GLYCYRRHIZINATE|, which is obtained from the herb liquorice. It is used in flavoring, particularly for masking the bitter taste of drugs like aloe and quinine. |FRAME: CPD-14483 glycyrrhetinate| is effective in the treatment of peptic ulcer |CITS: [1202773][762673]| and also has expectorant (antitussive) properties |CITS: [13683188]|. It has some additional pharmacological properties including antiviral, antifungal, antiprotozoal, and antibacterial activities |CITS:[14417970][6435904][19958823][21674592]|.</Comment>
